    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm working on a schema migration and i'm a bit stuck on the normalization part. can you walk me through how to actually get a table from 2NF to 3NF? i get the basic idea of removing redundancy but i keep tripping up on how to identify the dependencies. thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To normalize a table from 2NF to 3NF, you need to identify and identify 2 types of dependencies: horizontal (transitive dependency) and vertical (non-transitive dependency). Horizontal dependency occurs when a non-key attribute depends on another non-key attribute. Vertical dependency, on the other hand, occurs when a non-key attribute depends on the entire primary key.\n\nStart by ripping your table into three separate tables based on 2NF, then identify the relationships between the non-key elements. Generally, if a non-key element depends on only one part of the primary key, it belongs in a separate table.",
      "source": "target",
