      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In your table, a horizontal dependency occurs when a non-key attribute (also known as a non-key) depends solely on another non-key attribute, rather than relied upon the whole primary key.\n\nHere's an example: suppose you have a table of Employees, where one of the non-key attributes is a person's manager. Instead of just having a manager ID (or if you have a department ID, etc), you have a department ID and then you also note the manager's ID. To make it 3NF, you would normalize and split that into two separate tables: one with employee-manager relationships (using a separate primary key) and another just for departments.",
